WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
A classifier returns a risk score for a transaction.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
A generator writes an explanation containing several checkable claims.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.867
Fluent text replaces neither risk validation nor fact-checking its claims.

4
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:29.533
With logits two, one and zero, temperature one concentrates more mass on the first token.

5
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:36.383
Temperature two flattens the distribution before sampling.

6
00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:44.050
Greedy selects a maximum without sampling; it does not make the whole system always reproducible.

7
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:51.400
The model attributes an outcome to variable A.

8
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:58.250
A controlled intervention changes A while holding other factors constant.

9
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:05.600
Comparing both outcomes provides evidence; explanatory text alone does not prove causation.

10
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:12.950
The example has six true positives, two false positives and three false negatives.

11
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:20.500
Precision counts six correct alerts out of eight; recall counts six detected cases out of nine.

12
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:27.850
For text, add faithfulness and usefulness criteria: these fractions alone cannot evaluate it.

13
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:35.200
A workflow executes steps and conditions defined by its designer.

14
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:42.050
An agent can select tools or steps according to the observed state.

15
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:49.400
Both need validation; more freedom adds decisions that must be checked.

16
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:56.750
We require structured output, bounded latency and access to private documents.

17
00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:03.600
Reject configurations that violate requirements before comparing results.

18
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.950
The solution may combine rules, models and retrieval.

